# Binary assets must never receive end-of-line conversion.
#
# core.autocrlf is `true` on this machine. Without this file git decides
# text-vs-binary by sniffing for a NUL byte in the first 8000 bytes, so a PDF
# with an ASCII header and ASCII85-encoded streams is classified as TEXT and
# every 0x0A is rewritten to 0x0D0A on checkout -- shifting every byte offset
# in a format whose xref table IS a table of byte offsets.
#
# Measured 2026-08-09 in meyng-hub/sangoai, where this silently corrupted three
# PDFs including both halves of an EU funding submission. Git history stayed
# clean; the WINDOWS WORKING COPY was the broken one -- i.e. the copy a human
# opens and attaches. Files that happened to contain an early NUL survived, so
# whether an artifact was damaged depended purely on its byte layout.
#
# Deliberately NOT setting `* text=auto`: that would renormalize tracked text
# files wholesale. This declares the binary classes only.

*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.svgz  binary
*.mp3   binary
*.m4a   binary
*.ogg   binary
*.wav   binary
*.flac  binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.docx  binary
*.pptx  binary
